# KCD, 39 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device (-wgcopen), 2026-10-14, build ab1772e; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 91.0 s to 2439.6 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 39 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device (-wgcopen), 2026-10-14, build ab1772e; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 91.0 s to 2439.6 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 35
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.5
field_pull_wraps 40
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the second of two streams of 2026-10-14, from a relay launch of its own, 39
# minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured as the first: through
# Windows.Graphics.Capture with the mouse pointer in the picture, the frames a pointer move alone
# brings left out before the ring, and the frame pool on a device of its own whose textures the
# present opens through shared handles (-wgcopen). The arrivals are the game's pairs: 99.9% of
# the batches in the 60 fps seconds are pairs, 0.15 ms apart at the median, with no single alone
# on the cadence, and the 58 seconds in which a pointer moved in a menu kept their 60 pairs a
# second. Much of it is the dice game and a trader's inventory, in the regime, where the video's
# freezes bunch (the game drawing the same picture twice). The policy is the one the tree ships.
# The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 173 times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more 34 times an
# hour, in 54 bursts, 14 of them with a stall, and with no periodic stretch. The lock released 6
# times (9 an hour): at 555.7 s, 0.21 s after a capture gap of 41 ms, for 30 presents; at 749.9
# s, 0.29 s after a gap of 39 ms, for 7; three times at 1921.6, 1921.8 and 1922.6 s after a gap
# of 41 ms at 1921.3 s, for 9, 3 and 33; and at 2020.9 s, 0.28 s after a gap of 29 ms, for 2.
# The worst blend run, 35 presents from 555.7 s, is the first release. Of the 102 moves on the
# replay, 9 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 52.101 s, from the 2300
# marked frames in its first 38 s, which sit within 0.41 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 2387.4 s with no holes and ends at 2439.5 s of log time. Its first 38.4 s are the load list and
# the pause menu, so the cut starts at 91.0 s (video 38.9 s) and the marked frames lie before
# it. Its last minute moves between gameplay and the wait and sleep wheels and ends in gameplay,
# so the cut ends where the video does, at 2439.6 s. Every second inside the cut that falls out
# of the 60 fps regime is a hitch second, 5 of them in 5 runs, none longer than 1 s, so nothing
# was removed from the middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.5% against 0.5% (0.5% and worst run 35 on the dejitter arm, which is how
# the stream ran), worst run 35 against 35, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 38 against 40.
# Counted over this window, blends are 675 against 666, repeats 218
# against 219, skips 52 against 53, and lock releases 6 against 6, each at the same moment. The
# replay makes 102 moves, 6 of them late, and the field's log has 104 in the window. The 9
# blends, 1 repeat, 1 skip, 2 pull wraps and 2 moves by which the two differ were not traced
# present by present.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 35
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.9
min_reseeds 24
max_pull_wraps 38
extra_lag_ms 75
